# MEDINEXUS - Project Statement

## 1. Problem Statement

Hospitals handle different types of information such as patient details, doctor details, appointments, admissions, medicines and billing. Managing these activities manually can make it difficult to keep the information organized.

MEDINEXUS is developed as a basic hospital management system to manage these activities using Python. The project provides a simple menu-based system where the user can perform different hospital-related operations.

This project is made as a 4th semester programming course project to practice basic Python programming concepts and modular programming.

## 2. Scope of the Project

The scope of MEDINEXUS includes basic management of hospital information.

The project covers three main areas:

### Patient Management
- Register new patients
- Generate patient IDs
- Search patient records
- View patient details
- Change patient status
- Maintain basic patient history

### Doctor and Appointment Management
- Add doctor details
- View doctor list
- Book appointments
- View appointment records

### Hospital Services
- Admit patients
- Manage basic medicine records
- Create patient bills
- View admission records
- View billing records

The project is designed for educational purposes and does not represent a real hospital management system.

## 3. Target Users

The project is mainly intended for:

- Students learning Python programming
- Beginners practicing programming concepts
- Users who want to understand basic hospital management systems
- Students working on programming course projects

## 4. High-Level Features

### Patient Management
The system allows the user to register patients and store their basic information. Patients can be searched using their patient ID and their status can be updated.

### Doctor Management
The system allows the user to add doctors with their department details and display the available doctor list.

### Appointment Management
The user can book an appointment by entering the patient ID, doctor name and appointment date. The stored appointments can also be displayed.

### Hospital Admission
The system allows the user to admit a patient by entering the patient ID and room number.

### Pharmacy
The user can add medicine details and quantity to maintain basic pharmacy records.

### Billing
The system allows the user to create a bill by entering the patient ID and bill amount. Existing billing records can also be displayed.

## 5. Project Working

The project starts from `main.py`.

A main menu is displayed when the program starts:

1. Patient Management
2. Doctor Management
3. Hospital Services
4. Exit

The user selects an option from the menu.

Depending on the selected option, the corresponding module is opened. After completing an operation, the user can continue using the menu or return to the main menu.

The program ends when the user selects the Exit option.

